Subject: [PATCH] atl: the ActiveX container's sites (windowless site, frame,
 control site, container enumeration)

The container that AtlAxWin makes for a control answers the calls a control makes of it:
IOleInPlaceSiteWindowless capture, focus, device context, invalidate, scroll and default
window message calls, position changes; IOleInPlaceFrame (no tool space, no accelerators,
status text and modeless calls accepted); IOleControlSite (control info, lock, focus and
coordinate transforms between HIMETRIC and pixels); IOleContainer EnumObjects (the control)
and LockContainer; OnShowWindow. The container's state is now zeroed when it is made.

